<title>UK: Legal &amp; General down as CEO sells shares.</title>
<headline>Legal &amp; General down as CEO sells shares.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Legal and General Group Plc sank on Wednesday on news that the insurance group's chief executive exercised options, effectively selling 137,500 shares, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 1343 GMT, the shares were down 9-1/2p to 383.</p>
<p>&quot;It's just a soggy market,&quot; said one market maker. &quot;And (the chief executive) selling shares didn't help.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
